== Tear Falling Speed ==
'''Tear falling speed''' is a hidden attribute that determines how far above the ground tears travel after traveling for a short period of time, and in practice increases effective [[range]]. Very high tear falling speed makes Isaac's tears arc upward then continue along "cruising altitude" so high they can cross over [[obstacles]] as if they were [[spectral tears|spectral]], but they won't go through the room walls. Once the tears fall down, they will start hitting obstacles again. This compounds with the height from the tear height stat.
* {{dlc|r}} Items no longer give tear falling speed directly, instead tear falling speed is dynamically generated based on the [[range]] stat, [[shot speed]] stat, and tear height stat, in order to match the range stat in tiles.

