==== Notes ====
* Directional knockback affects most enemies, including bosses (except for stationary ones like {{e|Pin}} or {{e|Round Worm}}). Items (both [[trinket]]s and [[pickup]]s) cannot be moved by tears, except for live bombs.
* Knockback from tears provides minor crowd control for homing enemies like [[fly|flies]] or {{e|Gaper}}s, increasing the time it takes them to reach Isaac.
* Be wary of the natural knockback from tears when trying to dodge charging enemies (like the smaller twin of {{E|Gemini}}, {{E|Gurglings}}, and {{e|Leech}}es): The tears can push them off-track and towards the direction you are planning to escape to.

=== Knockback from Other Sources ===
Various sources also can cause knockback. This knockback is often a little shockwave that's emitted at a certain radius in all directions, most prominently from explosives, like {{e|Bomb}}s. Certain farts also create a knockback. Some enemies, like the {{E|Fatty}}, can fart, and Isaac can also do so with certain items.

[[Pickup]]s (including {{E|Chest}}s) are affected by this knockback; [[item]]s, however, are not.

=== {{dlc+|r}} Strong Knockback ===
Knockbacks from {{I|Belly Jelly}}, {{i|The Black Bean}}, {{I|Butter Bean}}, {{I|Divine Intervention}}, {{I|Hemoptysis}}, {{i|Isaac's Heart}}, {{I|Knockout Drops}}, {{i|Lil Dumpy}}, {{i|Mars|r+}}, and the synergy with {{i|Notched Axe}} + {{i|The Book of Belial}} + {{i|Birthright}} as {{c|Judas}} / {{c|Black Judas}} are strong knockback. They do not decrease from the enemy's friction and linger for a relatively long time once applied. Any enemy affected by it takes 10 + 2 × (floor - 1) damage upon being pushed into walls or obstacles. No other knockback can deal such damage however strong it is.{{dlc-}}

